#X msg 320 2546 === STEP-15-of-18 === THE NANO -- sweep every slider and knob now;
#X obj 320 2576 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2546 PASS IF: each control names ITSELF -- slider-1 to slider-9 then knob-1 to knob-9 -- and none reports another's name. Watch slider 9 then knob 1 especially: CC 9 and CC 11 are where an off-by-one shows;
#X obj 1100 2576 s \$0-say;
#X obj 140 2630 del 10000;
#X obj 240 2658 t b b;
#X msg 320 2696 === STEP-16-of-18 === THE NANO -- two faders at once then three then all nine;
#X obj 320 2726 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2696 PASS IF: two stay readable as stacked pairs -- three to five become small lines -- and nine shows the FIVE YOU TOUCHED FIRST with the rest refused. Rows must not reshuffle while you move things;
#X obj 1100 2726 s \$0-say;
#X obj 140 2780 del 10000;
#X obj 240 2808 t b b;
#X msg 320 2846 === STEP-17-of-18 === THE NANO -- press every button then all six transport keys;
#X obj 320 2876 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2846 PASS IF: all 18 buttons name themselves on press and nothing on release. The six transport keys report xport-1 to xport-6 on press -- no toggle and no footer change;
#X obj 1100 2876 s \$0-say;
#X obj 140 2930 del 10000;
#X obj 240 2958 t b b;
